From 3276df460489c59eb2b2f89c4f9af3a6eb6c0b77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam <sam@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:33:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(cli): keep a single leading system message and omit
 empty tools

OpenAI-compatible providers only accept a system message at the beginning; litellm rejected CLI requests once a system-role notice (error, tool cancellation, compaction status) or a stale serve prompt appeared later in the history. convertFromUnifiedHistoryWithSystemMessage now drops history system items and injects exactly one current prompt at index 0.

Chat mode also sent tools: [] because getRequestTools returns an empty list and only text tool mode suppressed the parameter. Empty tool lists are now omitted entirely, native tools still pass when declared, and chat mode is guarded at the request boundary.
