From ef9a495538e99b963850c3641315238eb46eb68b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam <sam@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:33:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(tools): recover tool calls polluted with native XML
 fragments

GLM through litellm/Ollama can leak its native tool syntax into OpenAI tool_calls: names become 'Read</arg_value>' (Tool ... not found) and arguments end with a closing XML tag or use file_path instead of filepath.

Add a shared sanitizer that strips XML fragments from streamed names, merges name deltas without appending closing tags, extracts JSON followed by XML, parses GLM/Qwen XML argument pairs, and normalizes common argument aliases. Use it in the CLI stream, in core tool lookup/parsing, and in the VS Code GUI streaming, generated-call, history and client-tool paths. Read-only CLI/GUI name differences (Read/read_file) are resolved without mapping write tools.
